course: dictionary
lesson: 5618
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the context to know which one is meant. The words around lightweight give you the clue. «She packed a lightweight jacket for the summer walk.» Lightweight here means not heavy, weighing less than usual.
explain: In sport, a lightweight is a fighter or rower in a lighter weight class. Sports people are grouped by how much they weigh, so the word is about a group, not about how heavy one person feels.
explain: As an insult, lightweight means someone who is not strong or serious, or who tires or gives up easily. «Don't be a lightweight!» is a tease, so the speaker means "don't give up so easily". Check the meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Lightweight means not heavy, as in «a lightweight bike».
fact: In boxing and rowing, a lightweight is a competitor in a lighter weight class.
fact: Informally, a lightweight is a person who is not very tough, serious or able to handle much.
fact: Lightweight materials, such as aluminium, are used to make things that are easy to carry.
fact: The same word can have a literal meaning and an informal meaning, so always check the context.
exercise: «She chose a lightweight jacket for the summer walk.» What does lightweight mean here? | Old and worn out | *Not heavy, weighing less than usual | Very expensive | Very warm and thick
exercise: In boxing, what is a lightweight? | A bell that starts each round | *A fighter in a lighter weight class | A referee who stops the fight | A glove that protects the hands
exercise: «Don't be a lightweight!» What does the teasing suggest? | Don't speak so loudly | Don't forget your lunch | *Don't give up too easily or tire quickly | Don't wear a heavy coat
test: «The bike is a lightweight model, so it is easy to lift.» What does lightweight mean? | Slow and noisy | Heavy and strong | *Not heavy, so easy to lift | Expensive and shiny
test: Ben says, «I was a lightweight in the race and gave up at the first hill.» What does lightweight mean here? | A heavy metal | A boxer in a light weight class | Someone very rich | *Someone who tires easily and gives up
exam: Which meaning fits «a lightweight bike»? | A fighter in a weight class | Someone who is not serious | *Not heavy | Very old and worn out
